   "source": [
    "from scipy.stats import spearmanr\n",
    "\n",
    "outcomes = {\n",
    "    \"Total Revenue\": \"total_revenue\",\n",
    "    \"Order Frequency\": \"total_orders\",\n",
    "    \"Average Order Value\": \"average_order_value\"\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "for name, column in outcomes.items():\n",
    "\n",
    "    data = customer_age_analysis[\n",
    "        [\"customer_age\", column]\n",
    "    ].dropna()\n",
    "\n",
    "    rho, p = spearmanr(\n",
    "        data[\"customer_age\"],\n",
    "        data[column]\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    print(name)\n",
    "    print(f\"Spearman ρ: {rho:.4f}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"P-value: {p:.4g}\")\n",
    "    print()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4a2cd9ce",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Result\n",
    "\n",
    "Spearman rank correlations found no statistically significant association between customer age and any of the three purchasing behaviour measures examined:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Total Revenue:** ρ = -0.0027, p = 0.6674\n",
    "- **Order Frequency:** ρ = -0.0065, p = 0.3054\n",
    "- **Average Order Value:** ρ = 0.0043, p = 0.4997\n",
    "\n",
    "At a significance level of α = 0.05, the null hypothesis is not rejected for any of the three measures.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Business Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "Within this dataset, customer age does not appear to be associated with how much customers spend, how frequently they purchase, or how much they spend per order.\n",
    "\n",
    "This suggests that age alone would not be useful for identifying higher-value or more frequent customers. Other customer characteristics may provide more useful information for understanding purchasing behaviour."
   ]
  },
