    "### Result\n",
    "\n",
<<<<<<< HEAD
    "Spearman rank correlation found a positive association between discount percentage\n",
    "and quantity purchased (ρ = 0.2871, p < 0.001), indicating that higher-discount\n",
    "transactions tend to involve larger quantities.\n",
    "\n",
    "However, discount percentage showed virtually no association with net sales\n",
    "(ρ = 0.0068, p < 0.001). Although statistically significant due to the large sample\n",
    "size, the magnitude of this relationship is negligible.\n",
    "\n",
    "Discount percentage was negatively associated with profit\n",
    "(ρ = -0.2035, p < 0.001), indicating that higher-discount transactions tend to\n",
    "generate lower profit.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Business Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "Higher discount levels are associated with larger purchase quantities, but this\n",
    "does not translate into higher net sales or profitability.\n",
    "\n",
    "Average quantity increased substantially among transactions receiving larger\n",
    "discounts, while average profit generally declined as discount levels increased.\n",
    "Transactions receiving discounts above 50% generated negative average profit in\n",
    "the observed data.\n",
    "\n",
    "The relationship between discount and quantity should not be interpreted causally.\n",
    "Larger purchases may receive larger discounts, rather than larger discounts causing\n",
    "customers to purchase more.\n",
    "\n",
    "Overall, the results suggest a trade-off between transaction volume and profitability:\n",
    "higher-discount transactions involve more units but tend to produce lower profit."
   ]
  },
